comments.content:
Publishing trusts `draft.outputJson` verbatim without re-running `validateDraftOutput`. Drafts persisted by earlier/legacy paths (or hand-edited rows) may hold an unexpected shape, in which case `output.items`/`output.text` silently becomes `undefined` and `activity.update` clears/overwrites existing activity content with `undefined` inside the transaction (not a runtime error, so the corruption is committed and only surfaced in the audit log). Re-validate before publishing and abort with 409/400 if invalid, e.g.:

```ts
const output = draft.outputJson as any;
if (draft.kind === "HIGHLIGHTS" ? !Array.isArray(output?.items) : typeof output?.text !== "string") {
  return NextResponse.json({ error: "Draft output is invalid" }, { status: 409 });
}
```

