The Prisma query is awaited without any try/catch. If the database is unreachable or the query fails, the rejection escapes the handler and Next.js returns an uncontrolled 500 instead of a defined response, and there is no error logging for diagnosis. Wrap the lookup (and ideally the whole handler) in try/catch and return a controlled JSON error payload.

```ts
try {
  const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where: { email }, select: { climatePassportId: true } });
