`checkRateLimit` is the synchronous in-memory (`local`) limiter. In a multi-instance/serverless deployment the bucket map lives per process, so the effective limit is `10 x instance count`, and the key degrades to the constant `source-unattributed` unless `RATE_LIMIT_TRUST_PROXY=true` — meaning all callers share a single bucket. For an abuse-sensitive, unauthenticated lookup route, use the distributed limiter, which fails closed in production:

```ts
const rateLimit = await checkRateLimitAsync(getRequestRateLimitKey(request, "summer-school-passport-id"), {
  limit: 10,
  windowMs: 60_000,
  sensitive: true,
});
