comments.content:
`await req.json().catch(() => ({}))` swallows malformed/empty bodies and converts them into an empty object, which then fails the Zod `superRefine` ("At least one of recordId, assetId or derivedFromAssetId is required."). A malformed-JSON client request is therefore misreported as a semantic validation failure instead of a parse error, making client-side debugging misleading. Prefer distinguishing parse failure explicitly, e.g.:

```ts
let body: unknown;
try {
  body = await req.json();
} catch {
  return NextResponse.json({ error: "Malformed JSON body." }, { status: 400 });
}
const parsed = EvidenceVersionCreateSchema.safeParse(body);
```

